---
description: Workflow for this time-boxed full-stack project
alwaysApply: true
---

## Project
- Frontend: React + TypeScript in frontend/.
- Backend: Python + FastAPI in backend/.
- Inspect existing code and scripts before making changes.
- Use SQLite when persistent storage is part of the agreed scope.
- Preserve the existing development startup workflow.

## Planning
- Base the plan on the agreed requirements.
- Identify assumptions and ambiguities that affect user-visible behavior.
- Keep the plan concise, with a data model and API contract.
- Use a compact Mermaid diagram when useful.
- Save the plan and milestone checklist in plan/implementation.md.

## Implementation
- Implement one agreed milestone at a time.
- Prefer small, complete user flows and minimal dependencies.
- For backend behavior, write focused tests before implementation
  when the expected behavior is clear.
- Confirm tests fail for the expected reason, then implement and rerun.
- Use an isolated test database; never reset application data for tests.
- Run relevant existing tests after changes.
- Verify UI behavior in the browser when tools are available.
- Pause after each milestone for my review.

## Debugging and verification
- Reproduce failures and inspect evidence before changing code.
- Add regression coverage for bugs where practical.
- Report exactly which checks ran and their results.
- Clearly distinguish verified behavior from assumptions.

## Documentation
- Keep doc/summary.md concise and update it at milestone boundaries.
- Keep installation and startup instructions in README.md.
- Do not add features outside the agreed scope.
